{"user": "Was there ever a risk that white could've flipped my corner or edge discs back somehow, or once I got a1 and h1 was I basically safe?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T21:54:59.686964+00:00", "assistant": "Your **corners were completely safe**: once Black got **a1** and **h1**, White could never flip those.\n\nYour **edge discs were mostly safe once connected to those corners**, especially the top edge. A continuous line like:\n\n**a1\u2013b1\u2013c1\u2013\u2026\u2013h1**\n\nanchored by both corners is stable \u2014 White can\u2019t outflank it from beyond the edge.\n\nBut in general: **edge discs not connected to a corner can still be flipped** later if White brackets them along the edge or diagonally. So the rule is:\n\n- **Corners: always permanent**\n- **Edges connected solidly to your corner: usually stable**\n- **Loose edge discs near empty/opponent corners: still risky**\n\nIn your finished board, Black wins **41\u201323**, so those corner/edge gains held up very well.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T21:54:59.686964+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T21:55:04.686964+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Common Ground Question": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "